/E (In Saudi Arabia, Loujain al-Hathloul and other activists led the Women2Drive campaign, demanding the right to drive and an end to male guardianship. In 2017, a royal decree lifted the driving ban, and from June 2018, women began receiving licences, a historic shift for the kingdom. Yet, at the same time, Loujain and several activists were arrested, detained, and )
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
551 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 303 0 R
/E (charged under vague national security laws. Her case revealed the contradiction between )
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [5]
>>
